(5654264, 819893, 87278, '<td valign="top">The angle is excellent capturing the sense of awe of a school kid! Congrats on the HS!</td>', 'The angle is excellent capturing the sense of awe of a school kid! Congrats on the HS!', '2009-09-20 08:52:49.000000', NULL, 0),
(5654354, 819765, 15690, '<td valign="top">I love this photo.  I gave it a 10, and left a message, but my fingers must have not been working so great, and the message never came up.  It brought back old memories for me when I went to Grammar school in California, especially the ink wells.  The boys would often try to stick one of my pigtails in the ink well. If I remember correctly, I think the desk top used to raise up, and we kept our papers and pencils inside. Thank you for helping me remember the good old days with your nifty photo.<br/></td>', 'I love this photo.  I gave it a 10, and left a message, but my fingers must have not been working so great, and the message never came up.  It brought back old memories for me when I went to Grammar school in California, especially the ink wells.  The boys would often try to stick one of my pigtails in the ink well. If I remember correctly, I think the desk top used to raise up, and we kept our papers and pencils inside. Thank you for helping me remember the good old days with your nifty photo.', '2009-09-20 11:19:39.000000', NULL, 0),
(5655857, 819765, 110186, '<td valign="top">I really liked this picture! Congrats on the ribbon!</td>', 'I really liked this picture! Congrats on the ribbon!', '2009-09-21 13:34:12.000000', NULL, 0),
(5656620, 819953, 59029, '<td valign="top">Greetings from the Critique Club!<br/> <br/>Initial impression: lovely building, pity that the foliage is in the way.<br/> <br/>Technical: Love the light, nice and soft, probably taken during one of the two daily golden hours or just slightly after.  I am a huge personal fan of the low pov.  Compositionally, the benches help create leading lines. I like the slightly tilted horizon, it adds some dynamism.  You don''t list any post-processing, and a shot like this usually looks best straight from the camera.  Having said that, a tiny hit of unsharp mask/sharpen edges may have helped the building pop a little more.<br/> <br/>Artistic: Nothing quite like going back to a place you loved (or at least liked, I assume) and trying to capture it in all its slightly wonky Greco-Roman-Gothic magnificence.  I think you did a very good job here, just would love to see how it may have looked from a worm''s-eye view and from underneath the closest tree, to eliminate branches.<br/> <br/>Overall: Pleasant shot, a good nostalgic capture.  Keep up the good work!<br/> <br/>Feel free to PM me with any questions,<br/> <br/>Susan</td>', 'Greetings from the Critique Club! Initial impression: lovely building, pity that the foliage is in the way. Technical: Love the light, nice and soft, probably taken during one of the two daily golden hours or just slightly after.  I am a huge personal fan of the low pov.  Compositionally, the benches help create leading lines. I like the slightly tilted horizon, it adds some dynamism.  You don''t list any post-processing, and a shot like this usually looks best straight from the camera.  Having said that, a tiny hit of unsharp mask/sharpen edges may have helped the building pop a little more. Artistic: Nothing quite like going back to a place you loved (or at least liked, I assume) and trying to capture it in all its slightly wonky Greco-Roman-Gothic magnificence.  I think you did a very good job here, just would love to see how it may have looked from a worm''s-eye view and from underneath the closest tree, to eliminate branches. Overall: Pleasant shot, a good nostalgic capture.  Keep up the good work! Feel free to PM me with any questions, Susan', '2009-09-21 22:53:54.000000', NULL, 0),
(5656762, 819887, 772, '<td valign="top">Greetings from the Critique Club...<br/> <br/>A score of 5.4 here is not terrible I suppose.  You showed a decent image of some of the stereotypical items associated with going back to school.  The lighting and composition on this image doesn''t really do much for me.  It''s rather dull and uninteresting.  Since I don''t have any information regarding your lighting technique, I can''t really offer you any suggestions on correcting that or making it more appealing.  I would have tried something a little softer or a larger light source to help with the reflection possibly.  I might have also tried a more dramatic lighting scheme along with a darker background to make the apple color pop a little more.  <br/> <br/>In the long run, this photo might have some significance in the world of stock images, but it doesn''t really speak to me at all artistically, and it doesn''t seem to provide any visual impact beyond what I would consider to be average.  <br/> <br/>What this photo does remind me of is myself when I was learning how to control things with my camera.  This is something I would have done myself to teach myself a technique, whether it be lighting or something else.  If this is the case with your image, I hope you were successful on that front :)<br/></td>', 'Greetings from the Critique Club... A score of 5.4 here is not terrible I suppose.  You showed a decent image of some of the stereotypical items associated with going back to school.  The lighting and composition on this image doesn''t really do much for me.  It''s rather dull and uninteresting.  Since I don''t have any information regarding your lighting technique, I can''t really offer you any suggestions on correcting that or making it more appealing.  I would have tried something a little softer or a larger light source to help with the reflection possibly.  I might have also tried a more dramatic lighting scheme along with a darker background to make the apple color pop a little more.   In the long run, this photo might have some significance in the world of stock images, but it doesn''t really speak to me at all artistically, and it doesn''t seem to provide any visual impact beyond what I would consider to be average.   What this photo does remind me of is myself when I was learning how to control things with my camera.  This is something I would have done myself to teach myself a technique, whether it be lighting or something else.  If this is the case with your image, I hope you were successful on that front :)', '2009-09-21 23:57:31.000000', NULL, 0);
